    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured audit event on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **A monotonic sequence source** \u2014 `AUDIT_EVENT_SEQUENCE`, a static `AtomicLong` allocated once per successful create, so `seq` increases monotonically across creates within the running application.\n\n2. **Event emission** \u2014 right after the existing human-readable audit line in `addOwner`, it builds an `OwnerCreatedEvent` and logs its JSON via the same `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n\n3. **An immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` record** \u2014 holds `seq`, `ownerId`, the primary identifier (serialized under `customerCode`), and `membershipLevel`, with a fixed `OWNER_CREATED` marker. Its `toJson()` renders a compact JSON object with proper string escaping.\n\n4. **A `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` seam** \u2014 the event's identifier value flows through this one method, which returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. This is the forward-compatibility point the spec calls for: when the customer code is later unified into the member id, only this method changes and the event automatically carries the member id instead.\n\nThe target test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
